# Regenerate PDF After Deck Updates

Whenever the investor deck website changes (`index.html`, slide images/logos, or PDF generation scripts), regenerate the PDF **only if the user asks**, or as a quiet final step when deck edits are done — never run Puppeteer/Chrome audits, mobile screenshot loops, or browser debugging sessions.

```bash
npm run pdf
```

This writes `MiJory-Wellness-Investor-Deck.pdf` using the screenshot-based WYSIWYG exporter in `scripts/generate-pdf.mjs` (desktop 1440×810 pages + clickable links). The generator also refreshes the footer **Updated … CT** timestamp in `index.html`.

## Requirements

- Do **not** use Chrome `--print-to-pdf` / print-media export.
- Do **not** use Puppeteer for mobile audits, screenshots, or layout debugging — fix web/mobile in CSS/HTML only.
- Keep using `npm run pdf` only when producing the investor PDF artifact.
- If `node_modules` is missing, run `npm install` first.
- Include the regenerated PDF in the same change set when committing deck updates.
